==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ru|en}} {{m|ru|перестро́йка||restructuring}}

===Pronunciation===
*{{a|US}} {{IPA|/pɛr.ɪˈstrɔi.kə/|lang=en}}
*{{audio|Ru-перестройка.ogg|Audio (original Russian)|lang=en}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{label|en|now|_|historical}} A [[program]] of [[political]] and [[economic]] [[reform]] carried out in the [[Soviet Union]] in the 1980s under the leadership of [[w:Mikhail Gorbachev|Mikhail Gorbachev]].
#* '''2004:''' [[w: Chris Wallace (journalist)|Chris Wallace]], ''Character: Profiles in Presidential Courage''
#*: Gorbachev would introduce '''''[[glasnost]]''''' (openness and freedom) and '''''perestroika''''' (economic restructuring) to Russia under his tenure, ultimately freeing thousands of political prisoners and dissidents and trying to address the shortages in food and goods that had become the hallmarks of the failing Soviet economy.
# The [[period]] of [[time]] in the [[Soviet Union]] during which these reforms were carried out and in effect.

